{"meta": {"name": "Sunburn device", "cloudId": "pxt/microbit", "editor": "blocksprj", "status": "unpublished", "targetVersions": {"target": "9.0.12", "pxt": "13.0.9"}, "comment": "Sunburn device firmware 3.3: the flowchart as blocks, laid out in 9 labelled sections"}, "source": "{\"main.blocks\": \"<xml xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\\\">\\n<comment id=\\\"note00\\\" x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"640\\\" h=\\\"470\\\">SUNBURN DEVICE  -  micro:bit firmware 3.1\\n\\nHow to read this workspace:\\nThe program is laid out in 9 numbered sections in two rows, left to right. Each section starts with a note like this one.\\nSections 1 and 2 are the whole program: 1 is the settings and start-up, 2 is the flowchart. Sections 3 to 9 are the parts the flowchart calls.\\n\\n 1 Start here: settings      6 Sound and servo\\n 2 The flowchart             7 Bluetooth and serial\\n 3 Buttons                   8 Helpers\\n 4 Alerts                    9 OLED screen driver (optional)\\n 5 Screen and LEDs\\n\\nPins: UV sensor P1, servo P2, buzzer P0 (optional), OLED on I2C P19/P20 (optional).\\nEvery function block has a comment: click the small \\\"?\\\" icon on a block to read what it does.\\nTip: do not use \\\"Format code\\\" or \\\"Clean up blocks\\\" from the workspace menu, that throws this layout away.</comment><comment id=\\\"note01\\\" x=\\\"900\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"730\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">1. START HERE: SETTINGS\\nThe \\\"on start\\\" block. First every setting the program uses (sensor type, servo,\\nscreen, UV bands, timings), then the start-up steps: this is \\\"Device turns on\\\" on\\nthe flowchart. Change your hardware and timings here and nowhere else.</comment><comment id=\\\"note02\\\" x=\\\"1850\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"5935\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">2. THE FLOWCHART\\n\\\"forever\\\" runs runFlowchart again and again. runFlowchart is the whole flowchart from top to bottom: read\\nthe UV sensor, sensor in range?, phone sending online UV?, UV index?, then one of the four branches, wait\\n5 minutes, reapply timer expired?. Every box and decision is a function here with the same name, in the\\nsame order as the flowchart. Read them top to bottom, column by column.</comment><comment id=\\\"note03\\\" x=\\\"8005\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"480\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">3. BUTTONS\\nA = done (sunscreen is on / going inside). A also skips\\na message scrolling on the LEDs, and while waiting it\\nshows the UV index and the countdown. B = wake from\\nstandby. A+B = device turns off, or on again.</comment><comment id=\\\"note04\\\" x=\\\"8705\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"1956\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">4. ALERTS\\nFlash and beep, tap the arm with the servo, and standby. Each one keeps going until A is pressed (or the\\napp sends \\\"ack\\\"), the device is turned off, or its time limit runs out. No answer within the time limit\\nmeans the device is probably not being worn, so it goes to standby until a button is pressed.</comment><comment id=\\\"note05\\\" x=\\\"10881\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"2298\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">5. SCREEN AND LEDS\\nWhat the 5x5 LEDs show, and what the optional OLED screen shows: the UV number, the band, messages and\\nthe countdowns. Messages scroll across the LEDs when there is no OLED.</comment><comment id=\\\"note06\\\" x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"3063\\\" w=\\\"485\\\" h=\\\"220\\\">6. SOUND AND SERVO\\nBeeps on the V2 speaker (or a buzzer on P0), and the\\nservo on P2 whose arm taps the wrist.</comment><comment id=\\\"note07\\\" x=\\\"745\\\" y=\\\"3063\\\" w=\\\"3683\\\" h=\\\"220\\\">7. BLUETOOTH AND SERIAL\\nTalks to the phone app (Bluetooth UART) and to the USB serial console with the same text lines.\\nOut every 2 s:  st=wait;uv=7.3;sen=7.1;onl=6.5;band=vhigh;spf=5400;spfn=3;fw=3.2;demo=0;pv=0.7;ck=183\\nOut on events:  ev=on  ev=off  ev=sunscreen  ev=reapply  ev=inside  ev=standby  ev=error\\nIn (one per line):  uv=6.5   ack   zero   cal=7   demo=0/1/2   power=0   debug=1   vol=180   screen=1\\nping   read\\nEvery line out ends with ;ck=N (character codes added up, mod 256) so the app can drop a damaged line</comment><comment id=\\\"note08\\\" x=\\\"4648\\\" y=\\\"3063\\\" w=\\\"3122\\\" h=\\\"220\\\">8. HELPERS\\nSmall tools used by the rest: sensor presets, the timings, sorting, number and time formatting, tidying\\nup commands, the line checksum, and the debug lines (send debug=1 to see them).</comment><comment id=\\\"note09\\\" x=\\\"7990\\\" y=\\\"3063\\\" w=\\\"6146\\\" h=\\\"220\\\">9. OLED SCREEN DRIVER (optional)\\nOnly used if you add a 128x64 I2C screen (SSD1306 or SH1106) on P19/P20. Draws text on it without needing\\nan extension. The program detects the screen at start-up and works exactly the same without one. You\\nshould not need to change anything here.</comment><block id=\\\"xRRgvHNlG#rZ^u`HECiY\\\" type=\\\"pxt-on-start\\\" x=\\\"900\\\" y=\\\"266\\\">\\n<statement name=\\\"HANDLER\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"}7p[#obkrwsG[8bRm}7x\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvSensorType</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"$!p@fu843P/.VDpM[=$S\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvSampleCount</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">15</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"r0agu6x/?cGK`ekk,3z*\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">soundOutput</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"L1nL[Yk[~^M8sl#3vMw4\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">soundVolume</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">180</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"QHHOk2C7#~daN5V15^IC\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">servoType</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"kax[+Ve6$8`f`V0NT^Y*\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">servoRestAngle</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">90</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"ZceNW.fmcPU7)C-h1yF^\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">servoTapAngle</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">30</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"o86?e)`eW-gMLPQy3$?l\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">oledMode</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"2=]21pJ;)jTz|W0(_;EJ\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">oledType</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"q,l6|}zKt1#?f0s~,,Jb\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">oledAddress</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">60</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"I!b3EWjgN^WsdLIe^}{x\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvLowMax</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">2</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"?;OpNt1%mKW;_Ed[#/X8\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvHighMax</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">7</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"T/7gB_Vyo%@cCXX$Pcj*\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvVeryHighMax</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">10</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"{%ndSjX|GIL!I1r@knHf\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">waitMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">5</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"`*Oh*rf/@TWb[_[/.W}N\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">reapplyHours</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">2</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"_$^14c:5Z%GrwBCJjQGM\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">tapMaxMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">2</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"ua^;#.76*r`u;;f|OX+Z\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">alertGiveUpMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">10</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"!mb0{4P_C5=Yg0r=p#L(\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">onlineUvMaxAgeMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">30</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"^YOln`tjfJbT.VA5;a9w\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">sensorRetrySeconds</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">5</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"+nKvR.f+P;p,qKQl7x*z\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">usbSpeed</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"]qdO}^(]d%+4JCx:{Ee4\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">firmwareVersion</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\"><field name=\\\"NUM\\\">0</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"text\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"TEXT\\\">3.3</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"d1Bsn[^t`G4kW4@/T=Wa\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"applySensorPreset\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"F]e$h{=?^]f;3k]PE5Kf\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"applyTimings\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"Ceik4jzr49[]2zjIv(vn\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"setupSound\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"j$weucE-eNYs#*GDhx^U\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"setupOled\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"C%z5^F2k1SYNLRm7_dp-\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"setupUsbLink\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"qL3VZR[ra*GxiE{Z:AsB\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"advertiseOverBluetooth\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"*f(ix~wdIzf%(p3Ezu/+\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"0\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"logic_operation\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"OP\\\">OR</field>\\n<value name=\\\"A\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"device_get_button2\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NAME\\\">Button.B</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<value name=\\\"B\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"device_get_button2\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NAME\\\">Button.A</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"}jIkJ]Jq,Gi9xw+wVTJW\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">demoMode</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\"><field name=\\\"NUM\\\">0</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"RgBL^9!Oe/~sS7O5.6mG\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"applyTimings\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"7I:R0~Ck=9f_;9q*}wa+\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"0\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"device_get_button2\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NAME\\\">Button.A</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"9Qp}.{WkW2cysVo$u?!I\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">showMode</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\"><field name=\\\"NUM\\\">0</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"c)WM5Chu$z88G5!07ZQw\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"deviceTurnsOn\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Hold B while switching on for demo timings: 10 s waits and a 1 minute sunscreen timer.\\nHold A for show mode: demo timings, pretend UV values that climb through every band, and\\nalerts that answer themselves, so the device performs the whole flowchart on its own</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">----- Device turns on -----</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">USB link speed: 1 = normal (115200), 2 = slow (9600). Use 2 if the app says lines\\narrive damaged, and choose 9600 in the app's Tools as well</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Safety limits: how long an alert beeps before giving up, and how long a\\nvalue from the phone counts as \\\"the phone is sending online UV\\\"</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Timings from the flowchart</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">UV bands from the flowchart (WHO scale), tested on the rounded UV index:\\n0-2 low, 3-7 moderate / high, 8-10 very high, 11+ extreme</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">I2C address: 60 = 0x3C (usual), 61 = 0x3D</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">1 = SSD1306 (most 0.96\\\" screens), 2 = SH1106 (most 1.3\\\" screens)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">OLED screen on the I2C pins (optional).  0 = no screen, 1 = detect it, 2 = always on</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Angles for a positional servo: resting, and the tap</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Servo on P2: 1 = normal positional servo, 2 = continuous rotation servo</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">How loud the beeps are, 0-255 (the app can change it for one session with vol=)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Sound: 1 = micro:bit V2 speaker, 2 = buzzer on P0 (a V1 always uses P0)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">One reading is the middle value of this many samples (kills noise spikes)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">UV sensor on P1.  1 = GUVA-S12SD / Crowtail / Grove / DFRobot / ElecFreaks\\n2 = ML8511 (SparkFun, Adafruit)   3 = sensors sold as \\\"0-1023 = UV 0-15\\\"</comment>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">START HERE. Settings first (change these to match your parts), then the start-up steps: sensor maths, timings, sound, screen, Bluetooth, then \\\"Device turns on\\\". Hold B while switching on for demo timings.</comment></block>\\n<block id=\\\"YXPLp6vzaln/E-76rAAV\\\" type=\\\"device_forever\\\" x=\\\"1850\\\" y=\\\"266\\\">\\n<statement name=\\\"HANDLER\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"7*ELL]h]yeT(Qz/UQQkX\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"variables_get\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">deviceOn</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"dihK4#Ime)4)i[kq#+JR\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"runFlowchart\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<statement name=\\\"ELSE\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"Q}T^R}@wgF.{bLk;x]}$\\\" type=\\\"device_pause\\\">\\n<value name=\\\"pause\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"timePicker\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"ms\\\">500</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Forever: one trip around the flowchart, then straight back to \\\"Read UV sensor\\\"</comment>\\n</block>\\n<block id=\\\"P.3J;;jDdW1pNLWrk#1S\\\" type=\\\"function_definition\\\" x=\\\"1850\\\" y=\\\"614\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"runFlowchart\\\">\\n</mutation>\\n<statement name=\\\"STACK\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"L-Pz1s^mrF1Td83HX-*G\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"readUvSensor\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"GAUm[:7xy?|]1Mn6Atz!\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block id=\\\"9V^%na-D$#R.H($R,Vlj\\\" type=\\\"function_call_output\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"sensorReadingInRange\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"Zz%5I0xizHXD`A2V:EQe\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"chooseUvValue\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"47{Q;2`{2yx?2_;dt~l6\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"showUvReading\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\